This idea has been in my head a couple of days.

we all know that when a PC reaches the astral plane he is considered
War as far as the other riders are concerned.

But say the fellow has been playing as a pacifist, or just wants a
change from the norm?  Why not have the potential to represent any of
the four horsemen?

So I think that the game should keep track of how you play, and then
turn you into the rider that suits you most in the astral plane.
Obviously, you'd have the other three to content with.

Each time you use a ring of conflict to make a monster kill another
monster, you should get one War-point.  Taming monsters, placating
shopkeepers and helping critters out of pits each lose you one
War-point.

Each time you use a wand of death or finger of death spell to kill a
monster, you should get one Death-point.  Raising the dead loses you
one Death-point.

Each time you use poison, potions of sickness, blindness or confusion
on a foe you get one Pestilence-point, but you can only get one point
per monster.  Every time you cure a monster that is suffering from any
status effect, or heal a monster, you lose a Pestilence-point.

Each time you go 1000 turns without any form of food, you gain a
Famine-point.  Each time you eat something you lose a Famine point.
(Ok, this one needs some more work, I think.  Does anyone have any
better ideas?)

When the PC reaches the astral plane, the game sees which rider the
player has emulated most, and awards him that title.  Whichever rider
you become is listed in your attributes+conduct.  If two or more rider
ideals are tied, the RNG chooses randomly.

Assuming you don't become War, you will have to fight or evade him in
the astral plane.  He should have at least two hits per round, and do
tons of damage.  Maybe he can summon nasties?

Finally, whichever rider you become, you get a small bonus.

War gets a 2-4 bonus to damage, and intrinsic conflict.
Death gets a small (5%-10%) chance of instantly killing a foe with each
attack.
Pestilence has a chance (15%-20%) of conferring sickness/poison with
each attack.
Famine gets 50-100 satiation points from every foe hit.  Furthermore,
he is immune to choking.

Hope you guys like the idea.



